From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:11:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: size the dedicated Mamba pool per align-mode snapshot

Port of the vLLM-MUSA 0.28 series entry 0138 (PR #285, regenerated by PR #289)
onto the 0.32.0 pin. Sizing the pool from one resident state footprint per
running request undercounts align mode: it pins one snapshot per cacheable
boundary and lets the in-flight batch hold one retired running block.

Derive the per-request block count from the Mamba cache mode, clamp it by the
block-table row width, and add the copy source/target pair when the hash
granularity is finer than the Mamba block. One helper now feeds the pool plan
and the admission bound so they cannot drift.

The 0.32 capacity estimate had no separate-pool accounting at all: it charged
one resident footprint and multiplied a mixed block count by one per-block
size, so the startup check and --max-model-len auto-fit could pass while the
real attention pool was short of one full-length request. Charge the whole
fixed Mamba pool plus the minimum attention capacity, as 0.28 does.
---
